[292.345, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 2/8 · Altitude\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I rebuilt `<workspace>/bayes.html` as the beginner-first explainer you described. It's still one self-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  contained file with no external dependencies. Both the independent calculation check and a phone-width and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  laptop-width look in Chrome pass. I haven't tested it on a real beginner, as we agreed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What it does now:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Opening:** it starts with your 1-in-100, 90%-accurate test question and four guess buttons. Answering\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  gives feedback that the true answer is about 8%.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Four dot steps:** 1,000 people, then who's sick, then test everyone (positives move to the top), then\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \"you tested positive\". The last step shows 9 really sick against 99 false alarms, and the answer of 8.33%.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Plain wording:** the text uses counts of people rather than \"prior\" or \"posterior\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Controls:** three sliders, each with a box where you can type an exact value, and five presets. The dots\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and the answer update live.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Formula:** it appears only after you reach the last step. It's shown in people and in probabilities with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  your current numbers plugged in, and hovering a coloured piece lights up the matching dots.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Checks:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Independent calculation:** a Node script reads the page's own maths and compares it against exact\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  fraction arithmetic. It covered 4,096 combinations of the three values, including 0%, 100% and tiny values.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  There were 0 failures, the dot counts always sum to 1,000, and nothing prints NaN.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Edge cases in Chrome:** I loaded seven edge cases in headless Chrome (for example 0% and 100%\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  prevalence, or no one testing positive) and found no NaN, Infinity or undefined anywhere. When no one tests\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  positive, the page says there's no answer instead of showing a number.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Bugs found and fixed:** the text said \"1 people\" and \"the rest are false alarms\" when there were none,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and the hover highlight was rebuilding the formula under the cursor.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Limits:** I didn't script typing into the boxes or clicking in a real browser, so those interactions are\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  untested. The number boxes clamp to 0–100 and tidy up on blur, but that is from reading the code. The \"does\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  a beginner understand it\" bar is unproven. On the phone the formula wraps across lines but stays readable.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Your first version is untouched in `.ambition/first/`, and this version is saved in `.ambition/steps/2/`. My\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  throwaway files (the check script and screenshots) are in `.ambition/work/`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
