[305.549, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 3/8 · Depth\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **The four statements**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **What a top practitioner would do that I didn't ask for.** Someone like an explorable-explanation\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  designer or a risk-communication researcher would test the page with real interactions, not just load it\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  with preset values. I admitted I hadn't driven typing and clicking. They'd also check that the page's own\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  words match its numbers. One gap to check: the question says \"90% accurate\", but the page never says that\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  means \"catches 90% of sick people, wrongly flags 10% of healthy people\". A beginner could miss the link to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the sliders. Third, they'd make sure the rare case, the one the page is about, is visible. At 0.1%\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  prevalence there is a single sick dot among 1,000.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **Rawest material.** The running page itself, driven through Chrome's debugging protocol (a real DOM,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  real events), rather than reading my own code. The palette values, run through the validator I skipped\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  earlier.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  3. **Methods and instruments.**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - A Node script that drives headless Chrome over the DevTools protocol: type into the number boxes, drag\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  sliders, click Next, and read the resulting text and dot colours.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - `validate_palette.js` on the blue, orange and neutral, in light and dark.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - A look at the 0.1% and 99% cases on a phone-width frame.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  4. **What shows it's right, other than me.** The protocol-driven interaction assertions, the validator's\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  pass or fail, and the earlier exact-arithmetic check. I re-run that last one so the new edits can't break\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the maths.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Rewritten task:** make sure typing, dragging and clicking all really work, including bad input. Make the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \"90% accurate\" wording line up with the sliders. Make the rare case visible. Validate the colours.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I'll start with the palette validator, since that's quick.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
