[386.864, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 3 report: Depth**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Real interaction test:** I wrote a script that drives headless Chrome over the DevTools protocol. It\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  types into the boxes, presses slider arrow keys, clicks presets, guesses and Back, and moves the mouse over\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  formula terms. All 24 checks pass, with no JS errors. This covers the typing and clicking I said last step\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  was untested.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Colour validator:** I ran `validate_palette.js` on the palette. The blue and orange pass colour-blind\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  separation in light and dark (ΔE 24–29, against a target of 8).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Looked at it:** I checked the light phone render, and the dark mode render with dark mode forced through\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the protocol.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Found:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Grey too faint:** the \"healthy\" grey was 1.6:1 against the page, so grey dots were faint.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **\"Accurate\" undefined:** the \"90% accurate\" in the question never said what that means, so a beginner\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  couldn't connect it to the sliders.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Lone sick dot:** at 0.1% prevalence the single sick dot was hard to spot.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Changed:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Greys:** now `#a8a399` for light (2.45:1) and `#7a756b` for dark (3:1).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **\"Accurate\" defined:** a line under the question says \"catches 90 of every 100 sick people, and wrongly\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  flags 10 of every 100 healthy people\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Glow on sick dots:** they get a soft halo, and the step-2 text says \"look for the glow\" when there are\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  three or fewer.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Limits:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Greys flagged:** the validator still flags the greys for \"reads gray\" and for contrast on the light\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  grey. That's intentional, since grey means \"not the thing\", and the dots are named in the text and legend.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Dark-mode lightness:** the validator's dark-mode lightness band flags the blue and orange. I judged them\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  by eye instead, and they read well.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **No real beginner:** it hasn't been tested on a real beginner, as agreed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The step copy is in `.ambition/steps/3/`. The test scripts are in `.ambition/work/`, and the first version\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  is still untouched in `.ambition/first/`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
