[430.705, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 4/8 · Challenge\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Assumptions I've been making, riskiest first**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | # | Assumption | Who set it / depends on | Risk |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 1 | 1,000 dots can represent any case the sliders allow | I set N=1,000. It depends on counts rounding to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  whole people. | **High.** Real rare conditions are 1 in 10,000 or rarer. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 2 | The page's factual claim \"most people say 90%, including many doctors\" | I wrote it from memory. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Medium. It's an unverified claim in the deliverable. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 3 | \"It's true whenever the thing being tested for is rare\" | I wrote it. It depends on the false-alarm\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  rate too. | Medium |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 4 | It works in browsers other than Chrome | I only tested Chrome. | Medium |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 5 | \"90% accurate\" means 90% sensitivity and 10% false positives | You and I agreed. The page now says so.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Low |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 6 | The formula should unlock after reaching step 4 | You asked for play first. | Low |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I'll test #1 first against real published screening numbers, which I haven't used yet. I'm running the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  actual page and comparing it with exact maths.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
