[1149.207, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 6 report: Judge**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did:** I built `judge.mjs`, which runs the same measurements on the first version and the current page in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  a real Chrome. It's a script, not my opinion. I also read the page cold, in the order a beginner meets it,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and looked at a phone-and-desktop contact sheet.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Check | First version | Current |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | External dependencies | 0 | 0 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Posterior vs exact maths, 144 settings | 144/144 | 144/144 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | NaN at slider extremes | none | none |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Jargon on first load | prior, posterior, P(H), Bayes | none |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Opens with the 1-in-100 question | no | yes |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Horizontal overflow, 320–1920px | none | none |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Text contrast failures (light / dark) | 3 / 0 | 0 / 0 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Slider update cost | 0.3 ms | 0.3 ms |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Found, and fixed:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Contrast:** the judge showed the current page was *worse* than the first version on contrast, with 11\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  failing elements in light mode. The cause was a muted grey for small notes, plus formula terms inheriting\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  it. Both are fixed, and the page now has 0 failures in both modes.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Spoiler:** the cold read found that the challenge card said \"only 8.33% of positive results are real\" on\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  arrival, before the reader touched step 1. The challenge, explain-back and summary cards now appear only\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  after step 4, and four new checks guard that. The safety card stays always visible.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Smaller fixes:** the sliders looked dead at step 1, so the text now says you'll see them at work from\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  step 2. H and E in the formula are defined, and I fixed the \"never cry wolf\" typo.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Where it's not better on every part:** I removed the first version's area (mosaic) diagram, its joint-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  probability table, and its \"condition on E\" toggle. That was a deliberate trade, to keep a beginner on one\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  clear picture and not two. It is a loss for anyone who liked the areas view. If you want it, it could return\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  as an optional \"see it as areas\" view after the formula. Tell me if so.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Still unproven:** whether a real beginner can answer the 1-in-100 question afterwards. Nothing here\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  measures that, and it still has only been tested in Chrome. The page is also about twice the size of the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  first (25 KB against 12 KB), which doesn't matter for a local file.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  All suites pass: 4,096-combination exact check (0 failures), 24 interaction checks, 32 red-team checks, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  6 bar-width checks. The step copy is in `.ambition/steps/6/`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
