[1390.162, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 7 report: Stretch**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did:** I added a \"▶ Play it for me\" button that runs the four steps itself. It skips the trivial \"picture\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1,000 people\" step, gives you 5 seconds on \"who's sick\" and 7 on \"test everyone\", then lands on the answer\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and unlocks the rest of the page.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Target and result:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | | Target | Result |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | **Stretch** | One click, answer in ≤ 12.5 s | **12.1 s measured on a real clock, 1 click** |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | **Fallback (yours)** | Step-by-step in about 3 minutes | Unchanged. 3 manual Next clicks still reach the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  same 8.33% answer. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Found:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Pause and interruption:** these were the likely break points, and they hold. The button turns into\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Pause. Pausing holds the step still for 8 seconds. Back, Next, a slider and a preset each cancel the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  autoplay immediately. Pressing Play at the end restarts from step 2.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Phone layout:** the extra button wraps to its own row at 320px with no overflow at any width tested.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **No regressions:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - the exact-arithmetic check passes (4,096 combinations, 0 failures);\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - 24 interaction checks;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - 32 red-team checks;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - 6 bar-width checks;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - contrast is still 0 failures in light and dark;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - and the new 14-check suite `play.mjs` passes.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Where it falls short:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Time, not understanding:** it's a measurement of time and effort to see the answer, not of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  understanding. In 12 seconds a beginner can see the answer but not necessarily absorb why. The guess, the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  challenge and the explain-back are still what teach, and the play-through is a preview of them.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Reading pace:** the 5 s and 7 s pauses are my estimates of reading time, not tested on readers. Slow\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  readers have the Pause button.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Still untested:** Safari and Firefox, and real beginners.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The previous version is kept at `.ambition/work/before_stretch.html`, and the step copy is in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `.ambition/steps/7/`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
