[1607.456, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Plan (as delivered).** `bayes.html` is one self-contained page that teaches beginners why a positive test\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  for a rare condition is usually a false alarm. It is built, checked and saved. Nothing is waiting on\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  approval; the open decisions are at the end.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ## Report\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **You asked for → it became**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Explain Bayes' theorem.** It became a four-step dot story that opens with your 1-in-100, 90%-accurate\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  test question and ends on the answer, 8.33%. It uses counts of people and no jargon.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Interactive visualisation.** It became 1,000 dots that regroup as you go, with live sliders. You can\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  also type exact values, from 0% to 100% with no NaN. Rare cases zoom out to a bigger crowd when 1,000 dots\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  can't show them.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Single web page.** It is still one file with no external dependencies.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Formula only after the idea lands.** The formula appears after step 4, with your current numbers plugged\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  in. Hovering a piece lights up its dots.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Goal beyond the goal: a beginner can explain it in their own words.** That added a guess question, a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  challenge card, an \"explain it back\" card, a label drawn on the dots, and a safety note.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Against the first version**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Better:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - no jargon on first load (the first version used \"prior\" and \"posterior\");\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - opens with the 1-in-100 question;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - typed values;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - rare cases handled;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - 0 text-contrast failures against the first version's 3 in light mode.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Gave up:** the area (mosaic) diagram, the joint-probability table, and the \"condition on E\" toggle. I\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  dropped them so a beginner sees one picture, not two.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Same on both:** correct posterior in 144 of 144 settings, no NaN at extremes, no overflow from 320 to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1920px, 0.3 ms per slider update.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Size:** the page is about twice the size (26 KB against 12 KB).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Outside check (ran in real Chrome; the runner printed ALL PASS)**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Suite | Result |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Exact fractions over 4,096 settings plus 5 real screening cases | 0 failures |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Typing, keys, clicks, presets, hover | 24 of 24 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Hostile input, URL injection, all corners, spoiler gating | 32 of 32 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Proportion bar fills its row | 6 of 6 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Play it for me | 14 of 14 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | First version vs current (above) | as shown |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Stretch.** The target was one click and about 12 seconds to the full answer, against 3 clicks and about 3\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  minutes. It reached 12.1 s with 1 click, and the manual path is unchanged. It falls short on understanding:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  12 seconds shows the answer but does not teach it, and the 5 s and 7 s reading pauses are my estimates.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Locked in**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Check scripts:** `bayes-check/` holds `run.sh` plus the six check scripts.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Notes:** `CLAUDE.md` says how to run it and what proved it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Command:** `.claude/commands/check-bayes.md`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Rerun:** `./bayes-check/run.sh`, which takes about 3 minutes and needs Node 22+ and Chrome. Set\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `CHROME=` if Chrome isn't at the macOS default path.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Saved copies:** `.ambition/first/` holds the first version and `.ambition/steps/2`–`8` hold each step's\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  copy. The `judge.mjs` comparison reads `.ambition/first/`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Assumptions I made (beyond your answers)**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - \"90% accurate\" means 90% sensitivity and 10% false positives, stated on the page.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The 5 s and 7 s autoplay reading pauses.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The cut-offs for zooming out in rare cases.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Dropping the area view.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The safety wording, which I wrote myself.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Decisions left, most urgent first**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | # | Decision | Options | For / against | My pick | Owner, date |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 1 | Test on real beginners | (a) 3–5 people, ask the 1-in-100 question before and after; (b) skip; (c)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  online survey | (a) is the only test of the actual goal but needs people; (b) is free but leaves the goal\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  unproven; (c) is wider but weaker control | (a) | You, by 2026-11-27 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 2 | Safety note review | (a) have someone clinically qualified read it; (b) cut to a one-line disclaimer;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  (c) keep as is | (a) is safest but needs a reviewer; (b) is simple but loses \"check again, not probably\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  nothing\"; (c) is unreviewed | (a) | You, by 2026-11-27 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 3 | Restore the area view | (a) leave out; (b) optional collapsed section after the formula; (c) separate\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  page | (a) keeps it simple; (b) adds a second view for those who want it at the cost of length; (c) splits\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the work | (b) | You, by 2026-11-20 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 4 | Browser coverage | (a) open the page in Safari and Firefox by hand and tell me what breaks; (b) leave\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Chrome-only | (a) takes about 10 minutes; (b) leaves your likely browser unchecked | (a) | You test; I fix,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  by 2026-11-20 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Metrics**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ```\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Metrics since 2026-11-13T00:39:42Z (cost: /cost, or total_cost_usd in headless JSON)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  total   in 182 · out 110.2k (think 39.3k) · cache read 10.02M · write 175.3k · hit 98% · 82 calls\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  model   sonnet-5-5: in 182 · out 110.2k (think 39.3k) · cache read 10.02M · write 175.3k · hit 98% · 82\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  calls\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ```\u001b[0m\r\n"]
